The main thing I see missing from that list is a ranged attack.  A
good stack of enhanced throwing daggers will save you quite a bit of
trouble during the stretch where you keep dying.

@digging for victory: you can get away with doing most of your digging
with a pick-axe or mattock.  Just be sure you have an escape item or
disable handy to give yourself a chance to switch weapons if you're
attacked while digging.

@#twoweapon: I don't know whether it's better than a shield, but I do
credit my own ascension to discovering how effective it is.  Possibly
it's only worth using once you finish ranking up all the weapon skills
involved and have both weapons heavily enchanted - but when you get
there it sometimes lets you kill boss enemies before they can teleport
away.

@SDSM: It's good, yes, but relying on its AC for survival is a trap.
Don't get overconfident just because you have it!


